{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0254", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-topological-flat}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:15b2cb52debfe3be85ff8ec3d880fb911e0f00f24edfdeaba60b495e64477a11", "source_text": "Topological properties of flat morphisms", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3450df38d0a1a7f9416eb5f9b581bc46e25700887e19562c48f284a0043ba5f8", "unit_id": "tag:0254:title"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0254", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6c8efc3362d3346c020900c868a37a9f9cc3ee503b60d7961799577e9ce790d5", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe ``recall'' below some openness properties that flat morphisms enjoy.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4be6b870cb2806002956d64fa930642c6bbbde33b3a4116de355336f74ef698b", "unit_id": "tag:0254:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "theorem", "parent_tag": "0254", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$Y$", "MATH_0002": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0007": "$Y$", "MATH_0008": "$f$", "MATH_0009": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{theorem}\n\\label{theorem-flat-open}\n", "suffix": "\\end{theorem}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1664c4352a793ba7943e4afca52d9cbbb5290a462190c3693127df05d8d6f61f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:85d09111bfa097d1d4322873417ce9f2ca234c1f8d7873190b392178c1461164", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a locally Noetherian scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a morphism which is locally of finite type.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a coherent <MATH_0004>-module.\nThe set of points in <MATH_0005> where <MATH_0006> is flat over <MATH_0007> is an open set.\nIn particular the set of points where <MATH_0008> is flat is open in <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3e5ba84e88b18ec8d56055d1f4e0c81e825b32b6f2aeb9dd9988436183074330", "unit_id": "tag:0255:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0254", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{more-morphisms-theorem-openness-flatness}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:35c5d2bd5a22163aba330029f5c7609227d43d92adb8f07a5bcd8aa844b3b534", "source_text": "See More on Morphisms, Theorem <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f870e96f338c74a8a65837888fc4e2425885fd496f077da0b4660cb1479edb7c", "unit_id": "tag:0255:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "theorem", "parent_tag": "0254", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$Y$", "MATH_0002": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0003": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{theorem}\n\\label{theorem-flat-map-open}\n", "suffix": "\\end{theorem}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:abd1406a4257199f65e6544045e2a5e69069d088852f8a60b3f516b5193526fe", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:48c6694727100aee4c2f6a4b7cc84f103009defae884a384d76b0e8792aaeb83", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a locally Noetherian scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a morphism which is flat and locally of finite type.\nThen <MATH_0003> is (universally) open.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0d51504cdeafa6faa5a4c2596e4f7fb1ef62e185cc4059ecd3f2cf82af8e4a6f", "unit_id": "tag:039K:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0254", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-fppf-open}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ab51b3fc5729081bc3da855453434d33f4ebed4397f5fd6f1eaf4b1f2ece948a", "source_text": "See Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:49833856461ac8c7d1a37ce897534d5f832dabf0d761aa0750dd5675b1520985", "unit_id": "tag:039K:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "theorem", "parent_tag": "0254", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{theorem}\n\\label{theorem-flat-is-quotient}\n", "suffix": "\\end{theorem}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0f1c67969a29b1747a33e5bc938ca190e5cb559ce2257534cd88d91dced9ae25", "source_text": "A faithfully flat quasi-compact morphism is a quotient map for\nthe Zariski topology.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:97eab318780d662597d9ac619f97e9ad847e4173bb48d6e09e0dec3834f3b40a", "unit_id": "tag:0256:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0254", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-fpqc-quotient-topology}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b37c49c35e9abdc5ee3649528d2a238cf7c2cf1e68d8d7be751146178a321a2b", "source_text": "See Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:49833856461ac8c7d1a37ce897534d5f832dabf0d761aa0750dd5675b1520985", "unit_id": "tag:0256:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0254", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c3309c80cc1fb297a2db0cd5beb3d3eda8cf01608ac86321e430279977de3c6d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0b6f1ebea6260e25d659cfb1ac04de89924f69d635fcbc6592165860c97c2c9b", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nAn important reason to study flat morphisms is that they provide the adequate\nframework for capturing the notion of a family of schemes parametrized by the\npoints of another scheme. Naively one may think that any morphism <MATH_0001>\nshould be thought of as a family parametrized by the points of <MATH_0002>. However,\nwithout a flatness restriction on <MATH_0003>, really bizarre things can happen in\nthis so-called family. For instance, we aren't guaranteed that relative\ndimension (dimension of the fibres) is constant in a family. Other numerical\ninvariants, such as the Hilbert polynomial, too may change from fibre to\nfibre. Flatness prevents such things from happening and, therefore, provides\nsome ``continuity'' to the fibres.\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bc74cfee92648c136c24f7cb4920c651f40c4f2e4f237d107dc4360afd54f39c", "unit_id": "tag:0254:prose-0002"}
